    {
      "scene": 1,
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 1.604167,
      "text": "How does Spring know what to inject?"
    },
    {
      "scene": 2,
      "start": 1.684167,
      "end": 6.838542,
      "text": "The order service constructor requests a PaymentGateway. Spring reads that dependency."
    },
    {
      "scene": 3,
      "start": 6.918542,
      "end": 14.584042,
      "text": "The bean factory finds compatible types. An unrelated logger won't match. Matching beans must also be eligible."
    },
    {
      "scene": 4,
      "start": 14.664042,
      "end": 19.921,
      "text": "Here, one eligible gateway remains. Spring supplies its instance to the constructor."
    },
    {
      "scene": 5,
      "start": 20.001,
      "end": 25.743083,
      "text": "Without an eligible candidate, this required constructor dependency stops context startup."
    },
    {
      "scene": 6,
      "start": 25.823083,
      "end": 33.677208,
      "text": "Our tests verify both outcomes. Qualifiers and primary settings can also affect selection. Match, filter, inject."
    },
    {
      "scene": 7,
      "start": 35.677208,
      "end": 36.767958,
      "text": "Thanks for watching."
    }
  ],
